  "sphinx_hop": {
    "status": "pending-implementation",
    "comment": "Part 1 \u00a75 CH-2 pins the per-hop key agreement: s_i = X25519(alpha_i, onion_i), and the hop keys (routing-info stream, the gamma MAC, the delta AEAD) via HKDF-BLAKE2s under the fixed labels sphinx-rho / sphinx-mu / sphinx-delta. There is no separate handshake transcript to vector (CH-1). These vectors are DECLARED PENDING, not hand-waved: this PoC implements no onion layer or X25519 (poc/dispersal.py: 'no onion layer'), so a reference output cannot be generated honestly yet. When a node implements the Sphinx layer, this entry is replaced by (alpha_i, onion_i) -> s_i and the three label-derived hop keys. Until then, two implementations are NOT yet proven to interoperate at the circuit layer (I-1), and this is stated openly (see Part 9 RI-10).",
    "labels": [
